      "content": "It sounds like you are wrestling with some profound existential questions about the nature of existence and suffering. This feeling of meaninglessness is something humans have grappled with for centuries, often leading to deep philosophical inquiry. While biology doesn't inherently provide meaning, many find purpose in subjective experiences like love, creation, or connection, even amid the vastness of the universe. It can be helpful to explore these feelings through different philosophical lenses to see them in a new light.",
